{"Title":"An Act to add law enforcement councils to the Massachusetts TORT Claims Act","BillNumber":"S1068","DocketNumber":"SD1494","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"MOM0","Name":"Michael O. Moore","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MOM0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T15:29:54.27"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"MOM0","Name":"Michael O. Moore","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MOM0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T15:29:54.27"},{"Id":"MRS1","Name":"Margaret R. Scarsdale","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/MRS1","ResponseDate":"2023-11-13T14:42:32.2933333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S1068/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Moore, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 1068) of Michael O. Moore for legislation to add law enforcement councils to the definition of employer under the tort claim law.  The Judiciary.","DocumentText":"\tSECTION 1. Section 1 of chapter 258 of the General Laws, as appearing in the 2020 Official Edition, is hereby amended by inserting after the word “Authority”, in line 48, the following words:- , any Law Enforcement Council established pursuant to section 4J of chapter 40.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J19","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J19"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}